      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've made a custom locomotion controller that activates arm movement when the user is doing the default gesture with that arm and, uhh...\n\n...it might look good and realistic for others, but it personally doesn't feel that good in first person. I think it stems from the fact that, in this state, your IRL arms have no input on your VR arms.\n\nI think the more adequate solution would be to improve the current running/walking animations to look better with common resting poses. Something like subtle arm sway when the user's IRL arms are down, but still affected by tracking. In the meanwhile, fully regain tracking if the arms are up. I think that could look pretty good and realistic while still maintaining a level of control.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-10-11T05:43:27.480Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "TYVM for reading! <3\n\nI've noticed everyone's running around with the default animation, leaning forward with their hands at their side, or in front of them on the table, and it can look pretty awkward!\n\nMost players don't manually pump their arms while moving, not to mention the arm movements probably wouldn't be synced with legs, at least not without looking down at the ground! So this is definitely just a simple visual fix that would greatly improve the look of movement for everyone in VRChat!\n\nHaving the option to toggle off Arm IK while running, leaving it  toggled off by default, and/or only enable it while holding objects would be wonderful!\n\nI understand some players would prefer to leave it on for pick-up (like weapons or other objects) or to enable it during hand gestures, so a mixed option might be the best solution for this feature!\n\nThe option in settings could look something like this, or better:\n\nToggle Arm Animations When Moving: \n(Off)/On/Enabled during Pick-up",
